course: dictionary
lesson: 9097
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Slushy is one of them. It can describe wet, half-melted snow, a soppy story, or a frozen drink. The words around it tell you which meaning the writer means.
explain: Look at this line from a poem: «Slushy green undergrowth Where the roach swim». Here slushy describes soft, wet plants by a river where fish swim. The clues are green undergrowth and the river, so slushy does not mean snow or a drink here.
explain: Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Try each meaning in place of the word. If one makes the sentence silly, try the next. Some words, like slushy, are also used in special topics. In a science text, «slushy forms» describes a thick, half-melted mixture, so read the topic clues carefully. When you are still not sure, check a dictionary.
fact: A word with more than one meaning has several senses.
fact: «Slushy» can mean covered in or made of half-melted, wet snow.
fact: «Slushy» can also mean soppy and too sentimental, like a soppy love story (informal).
fact: A slushy, or slushie, is a frozen drink of crushed ice and sweet flavouring.
fact: To choose the right meaning, look at the topic and the words next to it.
exercise: «Slushy green undergrowth Where the roach swim» is from a poem. What does slushy describe here? | Snow melting on a road | *Soft, wet plants by the river | Soppy and too sentimental | A sugary frozen drink
exercise: Mia says her book is slushy, full of hugs and sighs. What does slushy mean here? | *Soppy and too sentimental, like a love story | A frozen drink of crushed ice | Covered in half-melted snow | Soppy and too sentimental
exercise: Jayden orders a slushy at the fair. What is a slushy here? | *A frozen drink of crushed ice and sweet flavouring | Half-melted, wet snow | A soppy story | A small river fish
test: Dad says the road is slushy after the snow, so walk carefully. Which meaning fits? | A frozen drink | Dry and dusty | Soppy and too sentimental | *Covered in half-melted, wet snow
test: Tom says the film is slushy, all hearts and kisses. Which meaning fits best? | Soft, wet plants by a river | A frozen drink of crushed ice | *Soppy and too sentimental | Covered in wet snow
exam: Which sentence uses slushy to mean a frozen drink? | The pond was slushy with green weed | The love story was so slushy | The road was slushy after the snow | *We bought two slushies at the fair
